Why this is considered pull-based

It is called pull-based from the target environment perspective because:

GitLab does not need SSH into the server
The target server initiates communication to GitLab
The target server also initiates communication to Nexus
No one is remotely pushing binaries into the server over SSH

So the network pattern becomes:


What ports are usually involved

In this model, the target server usually needs outbound access to:

GitLab over HTTPS for runner communication, job polling, status, and logs. GitLab Runner communicates with GitLab to execute CI/CD jobs.
Nexus over HTTP/HTTPS to download artifacts through repository URLs or APIs. Sonatype documents Nexus APIs and CI/CD integrations for artifact workflows.
